```

More than one condition:
```jsx
<div className={`profile-card ${isOnline ? "online" : "offline"} ${isLeader ? "leader" : ""}`}>
```

KEY POINTS
- isOnline true → class="profile-card online"; false → class="profile-card offline".
- .profile-card.online (no space) means one element with both classes.

NOTE
A component's CSS file isn't private to that component. Once it's imported, its rules apply to the whole app. Unique class names like .profile-card are what keep styles from clashing.

IN PLAIN WORDS
Challenge: build an enemy list. App owns an array of enemies (each with an id) and maps it to <EnemyItem key={enemy.id} ... />. EnemyItem shows one row, adds a "boss" class when isBoss is true, and shows a Boss badge with &&.

KEY IDEAS
1. The parent owns the data array.
2. .map() turns each object into an <EnemyItem />, with key={enemy.id}.
3. Props flow one way into EnemyItem.
4. One EnemyItem = one row (<li>).
5. CSS pattern: base class + modifier class (.enemy-item and .enemy-item.boss).

STEPS
1. Put the data in an array with unique ids.
2. In the parent, map the array and render <Item key={id} ...props />.
3. In the child, accept props, set className for base and special styles, and use && for optional parts.
4. Style the base class, then the modifier.

CODE
```jsx
const enemies = [
  { id: 1, name: "Slime", type: "melee", hp: 25, isBoss: false },
  { id: 2, name: "Skeleton Archer", type: "ranged", hp: 40, isBoss: false },
  { id: 3, name: "Ancient Dragon", type: "magic", hp: 300, isBoss: true },
];
```

```jsx
// App.jsx
import EnemyItem from "./EnemyItem";

function App() {
  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Enemy List</h1>
      <ul>
        {enemies.map((enemy) => (
          <EnemyItem
            key={enemy.id}
            name={enemy.name}
            type={enemy.type}
            hp={enemy.hp}
            isBoss={enemy.isBoss}
          />
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  );
}
export default App;
```

```jsx
// EnemyItem.jsx
import "./EnemyItem.css";

function EnemyItem({ name, type, hp, isBoss }) {
