IN PLAIN WORDS
Wrap-up part 2 connects the Level Browser to real data. searchText changes on every keystroke; submittedQuery changes only on submit and drives the effect. The effect fetches, filters, maps the results to the app's own level shape, and the UI shows loading, error, empty or success.

KEY IDEAS
1. State in App: searchText (live input), submittedQuery (locked-in search), levels (results), loading, error.
2. The effect depends on [submittedQuery] and skips the run when it's empty.
3. API results are converted into the shape the UI already uses (id, name, difficulty, theme, description).
4. App shows loading and error messages; LevelList shows empty or the list.

STEPS
Inside the effect:
1. If submittedQuery is empty, return (no fetch on the first render).
2. setLoading(true) and setError(null).
3. Fetch; if !response.ok, throw.
4. Parse JSON, filter titles that include the query (lowercased), take the first 5, map to level objects.
5. setLevels(mappedLevels).
6. catch: set an error message. finally: setLoading(false).

CODE
```jsx
const [searchText, setSearchText] = useState("");
const [submittedQuery, setSubmittedQuery] = useState("");
const [levels, setLevels] = useState([]);
const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);
const [error, setError] = useState(null);

function handleSearchChange(event) {
  setSearchText(event.target.value);
}

function handleSearchSubmit(event) {
  event.preventDefault();
  setSubmittedQuery(searchText);
}

useEffect(() => {
  if (!submittedQuery) return;

  async function fetchLevels() {
    try {
      setLoading(true);
      setError(null);
      const response = await fetch("https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts");
      if (!response.ok) {
        throw new Error("Bad response from server");
      }
      const data = await response.json();
      const filtered = data.filter((item) =>
        item.title.toLowerCase().includes(submittedQuery.toLowerCase())
      );
      const mappedLevels = filtered.slice(0, 5).map((item) => ({
        id: item.id,
        name: `Level: ${item.title}`,
        difficulty: "Unknown",
        theme: "Placeholder",
        description: item.body,
      }));
      setLevels(mappedLevels);
    } catch (err) {
      setError("Could not load levels. Please try again.");
      console.error(err);
    } finally {
      setLoading(false);
    }
  }

  fetchLevels();
}, [submittedQuery]);
```

